  <event id="252">
      <start>15:00</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>H.2213</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Get ready for the PostgreSQL Extension Network</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>PostgreSQL devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The purpose of PGXN is to provide a central repository and distribution system for open-source PostgreSQL extension libraries. In its first iteration it will consist of four basic parts: an upload server, an rsync-able directory of extension distributions and metadata, a website for searching through extension releases and a command-line client for downloading, testing, and installing them.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will explain the current status of the project, how to install an extension and how to distribute your own stuff.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2521">Damien Clochard</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>